{"id":259,"date":"2020-11-18T18:12:05","date_gmt":"2020-11-18T23:12:05","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.fm1.dev\/about-us\/what-is-an-audiologist\/"},"modified":"2025-01-09T19:10:11","modified_gmt":"2025-01-10T00:10:11","slug":"what-is-an-audiologist","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/x-about-us\/what-is-an-audiologist\/","title":{"rendered":"What is an Audiologist?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https:\/\/schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"What does an audiologist specialize in?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"An audiologist is a professional who specializes in the diagnosis, evaluation and treatment of hearing and balance disorders.\"\n    }\n  }, {\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"What degree does an audiologist have?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Most have earned an Au.D. (Doctor of Audiology) while others have received a master\u2019s degree from an accredited university, where they received extensive training in the prevention, identification, assessment and non-medical treatment of hearing and balance disorders. They have to complete an internship, pass a national competency examination and obtain professional certification and licensure in the state(s) where they practice.\"\n    }\n  }, {\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"Where does an audiologist practice?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Audiologists work with patients of all ages, treating infants, children and adults for a variety of hearing and balance problems. They work in diverse settings like hospitals, schools, clinics, universities, private practices, VA hospitals, hearing aid dispensaries and otolaryngology (ENT) offices.\"\n    }\n }, {\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"What does an audiologist do in a day?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Audiologists are responsible for services such as: Fitting and dispensing hearing aids.\nAdministering hearing and balance tests. Assessing candidacy for bone anchored hearing aids and programming implantable hearing devices. Counseling patients and their families on communication strategies.\nDesigning and implementing hearing conservation programs and newborn hearing screenings. Providing aural rehabilitation.\"\n    }\n  }]\n  }\n<\/script>\n\n\n\n<p>Have you ever wondered what exactly an audiologist does, besides look inside your ears with a lighted instrument? If you have been <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-loss\/\" data-type=\"URL\" data-id=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-loss\/\">diagnosed with hearing loss<\/a>, you\u2019ll want to learn as much as you can about this professional who will be intimately involved in helping you come up with a solution that allows you to communicate more effectively.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Credentials Do Audiologists Have?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>An audiologist is a professional who specializes in the diagnosis, evaluation and treatment of hearing and balance disorders. To become an audiologist, you must now earn an Au.D. (Doctor of Audiology) from an accredited university, where they received extensive training in the prevention, identification, assessment and <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-aids\/\">treatment of hearing<\/a> and balance disorders. Our audiologists have a high degree of education as well as a caring approach. Audiologists must complete several internships, a residency year, pass a national competency examination, obtain professional certification and licensure in the state(s) where they practice, and maintain continuing education credits.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who Do Audiologists Work With?<\/h2>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"alignright size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-1280x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32286\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-1280x1024.jpg 1280w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-768x615.jpg 768w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-1536x1229.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-scaled.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/01\/1000010082-600x480.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Audiologists work with patients of all ages, treating infants, children and adults for a variety of hearing and balance problems. They work in diverse settings like hospitals, schools, clinics, universities, private practices, VA hospitals, hearing aid dispensaries and otolaryngology (ENT) offices. Audiologists are responsible for services such as:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Fitting and dispensing hearing aids<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Administering hearing and balance tests<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Assessing candidacy for and programming implantable hearing devices (e.g., cochlear implants, bone anchored hearing aids, etc.)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Counseling patients and their families on communication strategies<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Designing and implementing hearing conservation programs and newborn hearing screenings<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Providing aural rehabilitation programs<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Performing ear-related surgical monitoring<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Diagnose and manage tinnitus and sound sensitivity disorders<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Auditory processing evaluations and treatment<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>All in all, audiologists are the most qualified individuals to help you manage your hearing loss or balance disorder, and they provide an unparalleled breadth of care.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Call Elevate Audiology at <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-6611\">(864) 447-6611<\/a> for the Easley office or <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-4183\">(864) 447-4183<\/a> for the Greenville office for more information or to schedule an appointment.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Have you ever wondered what exactly an audiologist does, besides look inside your ears with a lighted instrument? If you have been diagnosed with hearing loss, you\u2019ll want to learn as much as you can about this professional who will be intimately involved in helping you come up with a solution that allows you to&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":111,"menu_order":4,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Who Are Audiologists and What Do They Do? | %%sitetitle%%","_seopress_titles_desc":"(864) 442-5555 | A South Carolina audiologist must undergo extensive education, training, and certification requirements. Learn about practice requirements here.","_seopress_robots_index":"","schema":"","fname":"","lname":"","position":"","credentials":"","placeID":"","no_match":false,"name":"","company":"","review":"","address":"","city":"","state":"","zip":"","lat":"","lng":"","phone1":"","phone2":"","fax":"","mon1":"","mon2":"","tue1":"","tue2":"","wed1":"","wed2":"","thu1":"","thu2":"","fri1":"","fri2":"","sat1":"","sat2":"","sun1":"","sun2":"","hours-note":"","footnotes":""},"service_tags":[],"class_list":["post-259","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/259","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"aut